 "free": false,
 "audio_url": null,
 "note_en": "Watermelon sellers often give a spoken promise of 保熟 (\"guaranteed ripe, or we'll swap it\"), and some customers take them at their word quite literally. The idiom 偷鸡不成蚀把米 (literally \"failed to steal the chicken and lost a handful of rice too\") means a clever trick that backfires on the trickster.",
